/-!
# The chart of `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ)` is the absolute `Proj` of a homogeneous quotient

Work in Situation 01NN: a scheme `S`, a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜` and a graded
ideal `ℐ` with quasi-coherent quotient pieces. `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/
RelativeProjGradedIdeal/Quotient.lean` builds `𝒜/ℐ` and the closed immersion
`Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)`. This file reads that closed immersion on a single chart: over an
affine open `U` of the base it is the morphism of **absolute** projective spectra attached to the
graded quotient map

`Γ(U, 𝒜) ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U`,

for `I_U` the homogeneous ideal of local sections lying in `ℐ` degree by degree.

Both halves of that statement are already proved in the sibling file — surjectivity of
`𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ` on the sections over an affine open (`…surjective_quotMkApp_app`) and the kernel
clause (`…quotMkApp_app_eq_zero_iff`) — and what this file adds is the **graded ring
isomorphism they determine**, together with its consequence for the induced morphisms of
projective spectra. Those are the second and third of the four inputs the `Not done here` section
of the sibling file lists for Tag 0801's relative `iso` clause.

## Main definitions

* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.sectionGradedIdeal`: **the homogeneous ideal `I_U` of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` cut
  out by `ℐ`.**
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.sectionQuotientHom` and `…sectionQuotientInv`: **the graded ring
  isomorphism `Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U ≅ Γ(U, 𝒜/ℐ)`**, for `U` affine.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.sectionProjIso`: the resulting isomorphism of charts
  `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜/ℐ) ≅ Proj (Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U)`.

## Main results

* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mem_sectionGradedIdeal_iff`: a local section of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` lies in
  `I_U` exactly when each of its homogeneous components lies in `ℐ`. This is the sibling file's
  kernel clause, read on the graded ring of sections.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.sectionQuotientHom_comp_quotientMk`: the isomorphism identifies the
  graded quotient map with the section-ring homomorphism of `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ`.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.chartMap_quotMk_eq`: **on the chart over an affine open of the base,
  the morphism `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)` is `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` of the graded quotient
  map by `I_U`**, precomposed with the chart isomorphism.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.chart_comp_quotAmbientHom`: the same statement written against
  `…quotAmbientHom`, i.e. against `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjBundleSurjection.map`.

## Implementation notes

`I_U` is defined as the kernel of the induced graded ring homomorphism rather than as the ideal
generated by the local sections of `ℐ`. The two are equal — `mem_sectionGradedIdeal_iff` says a
section lies in the kernel exactly when its components lie in `ℐ`, and a section is the sum of
its components — but the kernel is the description every consumer needs: it is what makes the
factorization through the quotient available with no further work, through
`Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.desc`, and its homogeneity is
`Stacks.GradedModel.isHomogeneous_ker` rather than a span computation.

`sectionRingHom_apply_component` is the exact analogue, for the homomorphism induced by a
morphism of graded algebras, of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.resRingHom_apply` for
restriction, and is proved the same way. It is stated here rather than next to `sectionRingHom`
itself because it is wanted only by this file.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)

## Not done here

No Stacks tag is claimed here. **Tag 0801's relative `iso` clause is proved**, downstream, in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/VanishingPresentation.lean`: the
chart-level hypothesis the reductions of this file leave is discharged there by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.ker_eq_chartMap_ker`, and the whole of
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.VanishingIdealPresentation` is built as
`…RelativeProjTwists.vanishingIdealPresentation`, on no hypothesis beyond Tag 0801's own. Tag
0803 is registered with that presentation discharged in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/FiniteTypePresentationOffSupport.lean`.

What closed the clause, on top of the reductions here: the chart comparison
`…RelativeProjTwists.pullbackGlobalSections_degreeSection_eq_zero_iff`, which composes
`…RelativeProjTwists.TwistData.ψ_chart` with the base change of the unit `M ⟶ i_*i^*M` along an
arbitrary open immersion (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartUnit.app_unit_eq_zero_iff`) and with
`…RelativeProjTwists.restrictionHom_app_eq_zero_iff_restrictionToClosed`; the resulting equality
of homogeneous ideals `…RelativeProjTwists.sectionGradedIdeal_eq_idealOfClosedSubscheme`; and the
absolute case of Tag 0801 restated at an `AddSubgroup`-valued grading,
`Stacks.ProjChartKerQuotient.ker_eq_ker_projMap_quotientMk`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open HomogeneousIdeal
open Stacks.HomogeneousIdeal
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

attribute [local instance_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

universe u

/-! ### The induced homomorphism of section rings, read on the homogeneous components -/

section SectionRingHom

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A B : SheafGradedAlgebra S}

/-- **The homomorphism induced on the graded rings of sections, read on the homogeneous
components.** This is the analogue, for a morphism of graded algebras, of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.resRingHom_apply` for
restriction. -/
public theorem sectionRingHom_apply_component (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B) (U : S.Opens)
    (w : A.sectionRing U) (n : ℕ) :
    ψ.sectionRingHom U w n = ψ.sectionPieceHom U n (w n) := by
  induction w using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | of m y =>
    rw [ψ.sectionRingHom_of, DirectSum.of_apply, DirectSum.of_apply]
    rcases eq_or_ne m n with rfl | hmn
    · simp
    · simp [hmn]
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add]; simp [hx, hy]

/-- A section of the graded ring of sections is killed by the induced homomorphism exactly when
every homogeneous component is. -/
public theorem sectionHom_eq_zero_iff (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B) (U : S.Opens)
    (w : A.sectionRing U) :
    ψ.sectionHom U w = 0 ↔ ∀ n : ℕ, (ψ.app (n : ℤ)).app U (w n) = 0 := by
  have key (n : ℕ) : ψ.sectionHom U w n = (ψ.app (n : ℤ)).app U (w n) := by
    simp [show ψ.sectionHom U w = ψ.sectionRingHom U w from rfl,
      sectionRingHom_apply_component ψ U w n, ψ.sectionPieceHom_apply]
  rw [DFinsupp.ext_iff]
  simp [key]

end SectionRingHom

/-! ### The homogeneous ideal of local sections cut out by a graded ideal -/

section Ideal

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) (ℐ : GradedIdeal 𝒜)
  (hqc : IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces 𝒜 ℐ)

/-- **The homogeneous ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` cut out by a graded ideal `ℐ`**: the kernel of the
graded ring homomorphism that `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ` induces on the sections over `U`. -/
public def sectionGradedIdeal (U : S.Opens) : HomogeneousIdeal (𝒜.grading U) :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.homogeneousKer (𝒜.grading U)
    ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U)

/-- **A local section of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` lies in `I_U` exactly when each of its homogeneous components
lies in `ℐ`.** This is the kernel clause `…quotMkApp_app_eq_zero_iff` of the sibling file, read on
the graded ring of sections. -/
public theorem mem_sectionGradedIdeal_iff (U : S.Opens) (w : 𝒜.sectionRing U) :
    w ∈ (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U).toIdeal ↔
      ∀ n : ℕ, (w n : Γ(𝒜.piece (n : ℤ), U)) ∈ (ℐ.piece (n : ℤ)).toSubmodule.obj (op U) :=
  (Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.mem_homogeneousKer_iff (𝒜.grading U)
      ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U) w).trans
    ((sectionHom_eq_zero_iff (quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc) U w).trans
      (forall_congr' fun n => quotMkApp_app_eq_zero_iff 𝒜 ℐ (n : ℤ) U (w n)))

end Ideal

/-! ### The graded ring isomorphism, and the chart isomorphism it induces -/

section Chart

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : SheafGradedAlgebra S) (ℐ : GradedIdeal 𝒜)
  (hqc : IsQuasicoherentQuotPieces 𝒜 ℐ)
  (hℐ : ∀ n : ℤ, ((ℐ.piece n).toSheafOfModules : S.Modules).IsQuasicoherent)

include hℐ in
/-- The quotient homomorphism is surjective on the graded ring of sections over an affine open of
the base. -/
public theorem surjective_sectionHom_quotMk {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    Function.Surjective ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U) :=
  ProjBundleSurjection.surjective_sectionHom
    (surjectiveOnAffineSections_quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ) hU

/-- **`Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒜/ℐ)`**, the graded ring homomorphism through which the section-ring
homomorphism of `𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ` factors. It is an isomorphism, with inverse
`…sectionQuotientInv`. -/
public def sectionQuotientHom (U : S.Opens) :
    quotientGrading (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U) →+*ᵍ
      (quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.desc (𝒜.grading U)
    ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U)

/-- **The identification of the grading of `𝒜/ℐ` over an affine open with a homogeneous quotient
of the grading of `𝒜`**: the inverse of `…sectionQuotientHom`. -/
public def sectionQuotientInv {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U →+*ᵍ
      quotientGrading (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U) :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.inv (𝒜.grading U)
    ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U)
    (surjective_sectionHom_quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU)

/-- The isomorphism identifies the graded quotient map with the section-ring homomorphism of
`𝒜 ⟶ 𝒜/ℐ`. -/
public theorem sectionQuotientHom_comp_quotientMk (U : S.Opens) :
    (sectionQuotientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc U).comp (quotientMk (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U)) =
      (quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.desc_comp_quotientMk _ _ _

/-- The inverse undoes the isomorphism. -/
public theorem sectionQuotientInv_comp_sectionQuotientHom {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (sectionQuotientInv 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU).comp (sectionQuotientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc U) =
      GradedRingHom.id (quotientGrading (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U)) :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.inv_comp_desc _ _ _ _

/-- The isomorphism undoes the inverse. -/
public theorem sectionQuotientHom_comp_sectionQuotientInv {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (sectionQuotientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc U).comp (sectionQuotientInv 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU) =
      GradedRingHom.id ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.desc_comp_inv _ _ _ _

/-- **The chart isomorphism**: the chart of `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ)` over an affine open of the base is the
absolute `Proj` of the homogeneous quotient `Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U`. -/
public def sectionProjIso {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ≅
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (quotientGrading (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U)) :=
  Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.projIso (𝒜.grading U)
    ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U)
    (surjective_sectionHom_quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU)

/-- The morphism `Proj (Γ(U, 𝒜) ⧸ I_U) ⟶ Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)` of the graded quotient map, which is the
shape `Stacks.ClosedSubschemeProjQuotient.ambientHom` has. -/
public abbrev sectionAmbientHom (U : S.Opens) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (quotientGrading (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U)) ⟶
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (𝒜.grading U) :=
  Proj.map (quotientMk (sectionGradedIdeal 𝒜 ℐ hqc U))
    (Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.irrelevant_le_map_quotientMk (𝒜.grading U)
      ((quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc).grading U) ((quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc).sectionHom U))

/-- **The chart map of `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)` is the absolute `Proj` of the graded quotient
map by `I_U`**, precomposed with the chart isomorphism. -/
public theorem chartMap_quotMk_eq {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    ProjBundleSurjection.chartMap (surjectiveOnAffineSections_quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ) U hU =
      (sectionProjIso 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU).hom ≫ sectionAmbientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc U := by
  rw [ProjBundleSurjection.chartMap_eq_map]
  exact Stacks.GradedKerQuotient.projMap_eq _ _ _ (surjective_sectionHom_quotMk 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU) _

/-- **The closed immersion `Proj_S(𝒜/ℐ) ⟶ Proj_S(𝒜)`, read on a chart.** Over an affine open `U`
of the base it is the morphism of absolute projective spectra attached to the graded quotient map
of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` by `I_U`. -/
public theorem chart_comp_quotAmbientHom {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    (relativeProj (quotSheafGradedAlgebra 𝒜 ℐ hqc)).chart U hU ≫ quotAmbientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ =
      (sectionProjIso 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU).hom ≫ sectionAmbientHom 𝒜 ℐ hqc U ≫
        (relativeProj 𝒜).chart U hU := by
  rw [quotAmbientHom, ProjBundleSurjection.chart_comp_map, chartMap_quotMk_eq 𝒜 ℐ hqc hℐ hU,
    Category.assoc]

end Chart

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGradedIdeal

end
